# No Dead Code

Every line in the codebase must serve the **current** architecture. Do not keep code around "just in case", for backward compatibility, or for a future that hasn't been decided yet.

## What Counts as Dead Code

- Backward-compatibility handlers kept "in case someone still uses them"
- Feature flags for unfinished work
- Commented-out code
- Unused types, functions, imports, variables
- Speculative abstractions — interfaces with one implementation "for extensibility"
- Fallback paths that never trigger

## When You're Replacing Something

Add the new path, delete the old path, update all callers in the same change. Do not leave `*Legacy` copies.
